:\n\nYou would use `ccs_mode=2` when you need to share data between multiple GPUs, and you want the data to be coherent across all GPUs. This is typically the case in multi-GPU systems where you want to share data between GPUs for tasks like:\n\n* Deep learning training\n* Scientific simulations\n* Graphics rendering\n\nWhen to use `ccs_mode=1`:\n\nYou would use `ccs_mode=1` when you don't need to share data between multiple GPUs, or when you want to improve performance by reducing"}